    cosmos_bc:definition "A surgical procedure to completely or partially remove a kidney. With a complete nephrectomy, the attached adrenal gland, perinephric fat, and regional lymph nodes are often removed as well. With a partial nephrectomy, the removed tissue contains the tumor and a rim of normal renal parenchyma only." ;
    cosmos_bc:ncitCode "C15284" ;
    cosmos_bc:packageDate "2026-11-02" ;
